1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,849
Office and community events involve different suppliers and payment
terms.

2
00:00:04,989 --> 00:00:11,505
SwarmPay lets AI prepare the plan, while your approvals and verified
delivery evidence control payment.

3
00:00:13,132 --> 00:00:15,449
This is a fresh PayPal sandbox run.

4
00:00:15,589 --> 00:00:21,320
Azure interpreted thirty guests, five rental tents, rain, and a fifteen
hundred dollar budget.

5
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:24,045
Its sourced plan totals fourteen hundred dollars.

6
00:00:24,185 --> 00:00:26,084
I approve those exact terms.

7
00:00:29,158 --> 00:00:32,794
The native PayPal button opens the tents merchant's checkout.

8
00:00:32,934 --> 00:00:35,489
I approve five hundred dollars of test money.

9
00:00:35,629 --> 00:00:39,810
PayPal captures it, and the application receives the native callback.

10
00:00:42,404 --> 00:00:45,030
The caterer has a separate PayPal approval.

11
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:49,544
Nine hundred dollars is authorized, while paid money stays at five
hundred.

12
00:00:49,684 --> 00:00:51,959
An authorization is not escrow.

13
00:00:55,306 --> 00:00:59,784
Now an outside Node client connects through the real MCP endpoint.

14
00:00:59,924 --> 00:01:03,571
It can read this organizer's plan and request a milestone.

15
00:01:03,711 --> 00:01:06,656
Its attempt to grant human consent is refused.

16
00:01:10,831 --> 00:01:13,670
The catering request returns ESCALATE and HELD.

17
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:16,509
No verified delivery receipt is attached.

18
00:01:16,649 --> 00:01:22,344
The record cites synthetic dossier five, because this demo uses a local
test authority.

19
00:01:22,484 --> 00:01:26,707
The authorization remains intact, and no catering capture is sent.

20
00:01:29,147 --> 00:01:34,499
The simulated venue signs delivery facts bound to this event, merchant,
and quantity.

21
00:01:34,639 --> 00:01:37,787
SwarmPay verifies the statement and time window.

22
00:01:37,927 --> 00:01:40,605
PayPal then captures nine hundred dollars.

23
00:01:40,745 --> 00:01:45,865
A signature authenticates the venue's statement; it does not prove
physical delivery.

24
00:01:47,492 --> 00:01:49,478
I repeat the milestone request.

25
00:01:49,618 --> 00:01:51,413
It returns the same capture.

26
00:01:51,553 --> 00:01:56,907
Tents and catering still total fourteen hundred dollars, with one
capture for each merchant.

27
00:01:57,047 --> 00:02:00,780
The evidence export verifies its application record chain.

28
00:02:02,937 --> 00:02:06,243
I ask AG Studio why the earlier request was held.

29
00:02:06,383 --> 00:02:13,763
Its analyst cites dossier five, explains the missing receipt, and
separates that hold from the later completed capture.

30
00:02:13,903 --> 00:02:17,189
The assistant can explain payments, never approve them.

31
00:02:23,491 --> 00:02:27,460
The pull requests also prepare the updated interface and gallery.

32
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:33,968
These are local review screenshots; the recorded sandbox flow uses the
existing public deployment.

33
00:02:35,595 --> 00:02:38,922
Try SwarmPay using the private judge instructions.

34
00:02:39,062 --> 00:02:40,275
AI plans.

35
00:02:40,415 --> 00:02:41,469
You approve.

36
00:02:41,609 --> 00:02:43,723
Payment follows verified terms.
